## 7. Schema Generation — `src/lib/generateSchemas.ts`

`generateSchemas({ post, slug, faqItems?, tutorialSteps?, tutorialMetadata?, videoMetadata?, galleryImages?, eventData? })`
returns `{ articleSchema, breadcrumbSchema, faqSchema, howToSchema, videoSchema, imageGallerySchema, eventSchema, websiteSchema, organizationSchema }`.

Note: `[...slug]/page.tsx` currently only calls this with `{ post, slug }` —
`faqSchema` is built automatically off `post.faqItems` (frontmatter), not a
separate param at the call site (the param exists for other routes/future use).

Other exports: `generateOrganizationSchema`, `generateWebsiteSchema`,
`generateJyotiSchema`, `generateRiSchema`, `resolveAuthorSchema(authorString)`,
`resolveAuthorId(authorString)`, `generateArticleSchema(post)` (standalone
version), `generateBlogSchema`, `generateBlogListSchema(posts)`,
`generateBreadcrumbSchema(items)`, `generateEventSchema(post, event)`,
`validateSchemaData(post)`.

Author resolution: `resolveAuthor(authorString)` from `src/data/authors.ts`
maps frontmatter `author` string → full `Author` object. Two fixed Person
IDs: `JYOTI_ID` (Jyotika Verma, default) and `RI_ID` (Gaurav Verma).

